knext bundled fix for vinext 1.1.0 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3774 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3773)
What it fixes: `_next/static/<buildId>/_buildManifest.js` was written with `sortedPages: []`, so
it never listed the app's Pages routes (Next.js deploy test custom-routes-catchall fetches it
through a rewrite and expects `/hello`). Next.js fills `sortedPages` with every pages/ entry
(pages/api included, as Turbopack does) plus `/_app` and `/_error`, in getSortedRoutes order:
a static segment before a dynamic one, then catch-all, then optional catch-all. Its client reads
the list through pageLoader.getPageList().
The client-build writeBundle hook now scans the Pages and API routes and passes them, in Next.js
format, to the manifest, which sorts them with a port of Next.js getSortedRoutes (the smoosh half
of the UrlNode route-validation.js already carries). An App Router-only build lists just `/_app`
and `/_error`, as Next.js always builds both. Page-to-chunk entries are not added (only Next.js's
own route loader reads them; vinext's client does not).
Port difference: none in behaviour; the dist hunks mirror the upstream source change.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3774.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

